 "notes": "Skill hits ONE ROW (3 squads side by side); the code places it on whichever row is hit. anchor_css = row centre (frame 172,330 -> css 195,363); per-pad pieces anchor on their pad centre (css 70/195/323, 363). tl = live row centre (or live pad centre) + offset_css (x AND y), so back/middle/front rows all work. f1 tp_burst (over): roar knot + starburst + side dust, centred ~90 css above the row anchor (the painting's burst sits above the squads); f2 tp_dust_f2 (under) dust wall behind the row, tp_ring1..3 (under, as in the approved composite) three open rings (scale out in order 1,2,3); f3 tp_smoke_c1..3 + tp_stars_f3_c1..3 (over, per pad), tp_dust_f3 (over, in front of the squads' feet) white dust burst + snapped bridge planks, tp_trench_f3 (under) trench + cracks; f4 tp_trench_f4 (under) trench stays, tp_stars_f4_c1..3 (over, per pad). Stun stars are tiny in the painting: code draws 3 bigger stars per pad (~28 css); the cut stars are optional.",
